            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>When Daniel Gygax, former President of Swiss biotechnet, and Letizia Vittorelli from the University of Palermo had the idea in 2005 to create the Summer School on Advanced Biotechnology, their aim was to exchange ideas and experience in a friendly and open-minded atmosphere to advance scientific knowledge. The network is a recipe for success: In 2017, it was the turn of the HES-SO Valais/Wallis to welcome the event to Sion from September 3 - 6.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
